      "id": "base_harbor_banner",
      "intended_filename": "base_harbor_banner.png",
      "requested_aspect_ratio": "21:9",
      "requested_quality": "High-quality wide decorative background; actual resolution must follow the selected funding source's model.",
      "prompt": "Create one premium ultrawide decorative background for a fantasy pirate stronghold game interface, in the painterly art direction of League of Legends / Legends of Runeterra, inspired by Bilgewater harbor. This is a background painting only, with absolutely no lettering, labels, numbers, logos, watermark, buttons, portraits or finished UI panels. Match the reference's deep navy and teal palette, antique brass and warm gold highlights, confident hand-painted material rendering and rich maritime atmosphere. Do not reproduce its icon grid. Composition: the left 60 percent and central area must remain very dark, calm and low contrast, with generous negative space for independently rendered headings, cards and controls. Subtle dark blue sea-chart contours and thin faded navigation curves blend into this quiet region; no readable cartographic words. Put the main visual story in the rightmost 35 percent: a moody cliffside pirate port, stacked crooked tavern roofs, a shipwright workshop, docks, rigging and distant sailing ships, soft sea fog, a few restrained amber lanterns. Layer a partially cropped antique brass compass and engraved fictional angular rune ornaments near the lower-right edge; these runes are abstract motifs, not text. Keep the central horizon quiet and the decorations mostly at the far right and outer corners. Use a very thin, understated brass flourish along the outer edge with a subtle worn-paper grain blending into the navy sea chart, avoiding a large heavy frame. Sophisticated cinematic lighting, readable silhouettes, cool blue shadows, restrained turquoise reflections, detailed weathered wood and aged metal, elegant atmospheric depth, premium painted collectible-card-game environment quality. Keep essential harbor motifs visible through a shallow banner crop centered on the horizon; no important elements at the very top or bottom. Dark left-to-right compositional gradient; no bright lights, dense linework or large focal objects in the left or center. Deliver a single clean wide image."
    },
    {
      "id": "base_action_icon_atlas",
      "intended_filename": "base_action_icon_atlas.png",
      "requested_aspect_ratio": "3:2",
      "layout_intent": "Three columns by two rows, six nautical fantasy icons; final crop regions must be measured from the actual generated image.",
      "prompt": "Create one polished nautical fantasy game icon atlas as a precise three-column by two-row grid containing exactly six square icons. Follow the reference's painted deep navy and teal backgrounds, antique brass frames, rich wood and metal materials, warm gold edge highlights and strong readable silhouettes, with League of Legends / Legends of Runeterra Bilgewater-inspired pirate craftsmanship. No characters, portraits, lettering, numbers, labels, logos, watermark, interface mockup or extra icons. Each cell has the same thin rounded square brass border and dark navy background, clear gutters and generous internal padding; objects stay entirely within their own cell. All six icons use consistent lighting, scale and visual weight and remain recognizable at small size. Top row left to right: weapon upgrade, represented by a forged cutlass with a small smithing hammer and restrained golden upward chevrons; hero secret tome, represented by an ornate closed leather spellbook with a teal gem and antique brass corners, no words or readable runes; cabin capacity, represented by a ship cabin doorway with a small bunk silhouette and porthole. Bottom row left to right: quests, represented by a blank rolled parchment mission chart with a red wax seal; navigation, represented by an antique brass compass rose and needle with no letters; expedition, represented by a small sailing ship riding one stylized teal wave above a rolled map. Use detailed hand-painted shading, premium material rendering, deep controlled shadows and concise coherent ornamentation. Do not claim or simulate transparency; retain the dark navy backgrounds inside every icon. No text anywhere. Deliver just the six-cell atlas image."
    }
  ],
